Settings and file policy: all v1 user preferences remain reachable. `Settings.vector_view` and `vector_backdrop` were old migration flags, deliberately retired by the v2-only settings policy; they are not new missing controls. `Selection.root` is likewise retired file state. Version2 preferences preserve extra keys, roots and window/scale choices. V2 additionally exposes voice-thread choices, memory budget, per-instrument view choices, CC/Program articulation drivers and typed processor inspection. Browser index caches, path identity and library-resource resolution use v2 implementations; no v1 file-format compatibility is introduced.

Removed command census: `Remap`, `Learn`, `KeepOriginal`, `ResetChannel`, `TakePart`, and `SplitVelocities` map to `inside::ArtAction` (ResetRow/Clear/Learn/Keep/Include/Split) and stable articulation overlays. `Script` maps to authored IR menu/widget control submission (`generated.rs`, `ir_view.rs`); `StripRename`/`StripReset` map to native node IDs. `BusPort` maps to host-bus output picking; `StripRoute` was the missing context shortcut repaired here. Mic bus/name state now lives in NodeMix/MixTree. Physical registry persistence covers supported engine parameters, but full v1 engine/delay/IR asset recall still needs authored session evidence. No removed enum name alone establishes a regression.

UVI library discovery uses the native UFS path and version2 settings; the third-party reader/opener remains banned. This is source availability, not complete UVI/Kontakt library parity. Authored assets, script position/hide/z-order/pages and fluid interaction belong to the unified intrinsic UI gate. No substitute panels or heuristic UI are added.

Validation and receipt: `/mnt/Windows11/DEV_WORKSPACE/kontra-runs/w13-settings-parity-393`. The pre-correction shared-target compile failure is excluded; the timestamp retry was cancelled before execution. The final fixture supplies real native editor IR, and the mixer case starts from the Effects subtab before invoking Edit sound. A preliminary empty-instrument fixture and the first port compile failure are retained separately; the native-fixture baseline and final GREEN are the decisive pair. Only corrected per-worktree runtime tests count as RED/GREEN. Targeted menu tests exercise mouse-opened mixer context menus and keyboard menu activation, requested-part selection and saved part/host-bus routing. Trusted native-fixture baseline: 0 passed, 3 failed (exit101). Corrected per-worktree candidate: 3 menu + 2 existing mixer + 1 timing-menu tests passed, no failures; root `cargo test --profile ci --features shots --no-run` passed. Routing/timing shots were retained, and the routing shot was visually checked. Exact results and log hashes are recorded in READY.json.

